---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
import checks from '../../../../../public/equipment/03-05/verification.json';
import m from '../../../../../public/equipment/03-05/interactions.json';
const a='/equipment/03-05/',photo='https://www.nanogune.eu/en/nanogune-at-a-glance/facilities-equipment/equipment/ald-cambridge-nanotech-savannah-s100',scale='https://mrl.illinois.edu/facilities/equipment/savannah-s100-atomic-layer-deposition-cambridge-nanotech';
const display=x=>Object.entries(x??{}).map(([k,v])=>k+': '+String(v)).join('; ');
---
<Layout pageTitle="Savannah S100 dry carrier gauge" subtitle="" description="Inspect a de-energized S100 cabinet and test inert disc alignment in a separate dry gauge." wide={true}>
<article id="s100" class="equipment"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/03-05/">← Equipment 03-05</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#s100-checks">Verification</a></nav>
<header><p class="eq-meta">03-05 / Savannah S100 / De-energized visual study</p><h2>Savannah S100</h2><p>Inspect the Cambridge NanoTech cabinet and use a separate inert-disc alignment gauge. The 100 mm reference disc fits with 1 mm of radial margin at a 5 mm center offset. The cabinet remains static.</p></header>
<div class="e-grid"><section class="e-card"><h3>01 · Inspect the cabinet and gauge</h3><div id="s100-views" class="e-row">{['Bench','Front','Guard','Gauge'].map(k=><button type="button" data-view={k.toLowerCase()}>{k}</button>)}<button id="s100-xr" type="button" disabled>VR unavailable</button></div>
<canvas id="s100-model" aria-label="Orbitable static instrument cabinet and detached dry alignment gauge"></canvas><p id="s100-asset" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><p class="e-hint">Click the round external gauge to position a dummy; click the dummy or the yellow fixture button to check it. Orbit, zoom or choose close-ups. The cabinet handle and top guard are fixed.</p></section>
<section class="e-card"><h3>02 · Check alignment</h3><div class="e-row"><button id="s100-place" type="button">Position inert dummy</button><button id="s100-example" class="e-run" type="button">Position and check example</button></div>
<form id="s100-form" novalidate><div class="e-fields"><label>Dummy ID<input name="dummyId" value="dry-disc-01" maxlength="96"/></label>{[['diameterMm','Disc diameter (mm)',100,50,140],['offsetXmm','X offset (mm)',3,-25,25],['offsetZmm','Z offset (mm)',4,-25,25]].map(([k,t,v,min,max])=><label>{t}<input name={k} type="number" min={min} max={max} step="any" value={v}/></label>)}</div>
<div class="e-row"><button id="s100-check" class="e-run" type="submit">Check planar fit</button><button id="s100-offset" type="button">Set larger offset</button><button id="s100-reset" type="button">Reset</button></div></form><p id="s100-status" role="status">No dummy positioned.</p></section></div>
<section class="e-card"><h3>03 · Read signed radial margin</h3><p id="s100-result" role="status">No fit result.</p><div class="e-row"><button id="s100-json" disabled>Dry fit JSON</button></div><p>Margin = 56 mm − disc radius − √(X² + Z²). Positive means the outlined circle fits by that radial distance; zero is nominal tangency. The 112 mm gauge is an original external prop, not an S100 chamber dimension or accessory. <a href={a+'example-fit.json'}>Example result</a>.</p></section>
<section><h3>Geometry references</h3><div class="e-grid"><figure><img src={a+'original-front.svg'} width="760" height="450" alt="Original metric S100 front and raised circular guard"/><figcaption>Original rendering based on <a href={photo}>CIC nanoGUNE’s photograph of its Savannah S100</a>, showing the narrow metal cabinet, fixed handle, circular top assembly and guard. Cabinet envelope is an illustrative design estimate (485 mm wide, 493 mm deep and about 1,020 mm high), not measured or manufacturer-certified.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src={a+'original-work.svg'} width="760" height="450" alt="Original dry fit plate and inert circular dummy on a detached stand"/><figcaption>Detached educational gauge. <a href={scale}>Illinois MRL lists a nominal 4-inch sample size</a>; the 100 mm-class dummy uses an original exact diameter and contains no applied layer.</figcaption></figure></div>
<p>This pass models geometry only. It does not reproduce internals, plumbing, cabinet access, programs, material processing or layer growth. The register’s layer-growth and cycle acceptance is outside the scope. Results are simulated fit checks, not suitability for using the actual instrument.</p></section>
<section id="s100-checks"><h3>Verification and files</h3><div class="e-over"><table><thead><tr><th>Case</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead><tbody>{checks.map(x=><tr><td>{x.id}</td><td>{display(x.expected)}</td><td>{display(x.actual)}</td><td>{x.pass?'Pass':'Fail'}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
<p><a href={a+'reference-plan.json'}>Predeclared cases</a> · <a href={a+'verification.json'}>Verification data</a> · <a href={a+'savannah-s100.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={a+'geometry-source.mjs'}>Editable geometry</a> + <a href={a+'make-model.mjs'}>generator</a> + <a href={a+'mesh-writer.mjs'}>mesh writer</a> · <a href={a+'interactions.json'}>Named targets</a>. {m.triangles.toLocaleString()} triangles and {m.draws} draw primitives; optional WebXR, physical headset untested.</p></section></article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/03-05/client.mjs';</script>
<style>
#s100 header{max-width:73ch;padding:1.3rem 0}#s100 h2{font-size:clamp(2rem,6vw,4rem);margin:.2rem 0}#s100 section{margin:1rem 0}.e-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}.e-card{border:1px solid var(--border);padding:.8rem;min-width:0}.e-card h3{margin:.3rem 0}.e-row{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.4rem;margin:.5rem 0}.e-fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.55rem}.e-fields label{display:grid;gap:.2rem}.e-fields input,#s100 button{min-width:0;min-height:2.45rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:3px;background:var(--panel);color:var(--text);font:inherit;padding:.3rem .5rem;box-sizing:border-box}#s100 button:disabled{opacity:.52}.e-run{background:#3d596e!important;color:white!important}#s100-model{width:100%;height:clamp(280px,34vw,440px);display:block;background:#ebe8e0;touch-action:none}#s100-chart{width:100%;max-height:16rem}.e-over{overflow:auto}#s100 table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:.85rem}#s100 td,#s100 th{text-align:left;padding:.45rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}#s100 figure{margin:0}#s100 img{width:100%;height:auto}@media(max-width:820px){.e-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.e-fields{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}}
#s100 caption{text-align:left}#s100 input,#s100 select,#s100 button{min-width:0}#s100 .e-hint{font-size:.92rem}</style>
